WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:33.650
Faith seems to play a role in expanding imagination, but what, how, what, how do you think this works, do you think more of it can be done? And how do you, how do you suggest

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:40.650
that we get people to practically understand what is at stake and how we can do something about it?

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:51.510
I, probably the best thing I've learned the last ten years about faith

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:54.040
comes from First Thessalonians in the, in

00:00:54.040 --> 00:01:00.150
the New Testament, where Paul's writing a letter and

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:04.800
he's writing the letter to the Thessalonians and he's saying that, that when Silvanus, Timothy, 

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.410
and I came to you

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:09.660
we had power,

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:11.400
we had the Holy Spirit,

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:13.990
and we had true conviction.

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:18.990
And what I learned from that is the best thing I've learned in ten years about faith

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:20.520
and, and growing

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:21.650
is where I,

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:27.240
when I go to a difficult place or I'm in a difficult situation, I take a prayer partner with me.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:29.930
This is a practical thing

00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:30.920
and it's not

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:34.770
it's, it's something that Jesus did, Paul did.

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:36.590
They were very seldom ever alone.

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:39.530
The only time they were alone when they were with God.

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:41.120
But they always took people with them

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:45.540
and Paul says, you know,

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:47.500
do this,

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:49.890
when two or more are gathered together I'm there,

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:54.170
if you do this you have power. And I can't tell you how many times I've been to North

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:54.609
Korea,

00:01:54.609 --> 00:01:56.500
the Congo,

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:01.410
when you meet, and you go to difficult places and you see people dying and

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:05.840
the power of two or more together and

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:09.729
what happens is every morning we get up if we're on a trip and we,

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:14.449
we would pray before the day would start and then when we go, if I'm meeting with somebody

00:02:14.449 --> 00:02:19.209
that's really poor, a mother or something, or I'm meeting with the prime minister,

00:02:19.209 --> 00:02:24.020
my friend, who is with me, I just introduce him as an agriculture specialist, which he was,

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:25.370
but he's praying.

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:26.319
He doesn't tell

00:02:26.319 --> 00:02:27.609
the person he's praying.

00:02:27.609 --> 00:02:28.769
He prays.

00:02:28.769 --> 00:02:30.340
I can't tell you

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:33.189
how many times

00:02:33.189 --> 00:02:37.009
I've seen that conversation turn around,

00:02:37.009 --> 00:02:39.449
where we leave the country and

00:02:39.449 --> 00:02:41.910
not because we have a sparkling personalities.

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:45.959
It's because, you know, you people are different, this is really, this is

00:02:45.959 --> 00:02:49.479
some of the best conversations I ever had. It's because

00:02:49.479 --> 00:02:55.689
of what I learned from Paul that when you take a prayer partner you have support. You're stronger.

00:02:55.689 --> 00:02:57.859
You're, you have the power with you

00:02:57.859 --> 00:02:58.749
and it's,

00:02:58.749 --> 00:03:05.749
it really works. I mean it's the most interesting thing that I've learned the last ten. It's so simple that

00:03:05.759 --> 00:03:08.349
there's so many lessons that we can learn
from the,

00:03:08.349 --> 00:03:12.779
from the scriptures but we, we bypass it because they're too simple

00:03:12.779 --> 00:03:14.179
they, they don't work.

00:03:14.179 --> 00:03:15.849
And I find

00:03:15.849 --> 00:03:17.890
and when I face a difficult situation

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:19.149
like a fast

00:03:19.149 --> 00:03:22.529
if I ask other people, if I get people to pray with me,

00:03:22.529 --> 00:03:25.189
I don't have to announce it to the world.

00:03:25.189 --> 00:03:32.189
The power is there. Is it okay if I ask just a quick follow-up question? What if people don't see their fast as necessary? How do you, how do you get either faith or something else to help people to see that something's going on? Well,

00:03:40.239 --> 00:03:44.569
you know what, I do the things in front of me. I don't try to save everybody.

00:03:44.569 --> 00:03:46.859
I try to,

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:49.009
you know, I just go

00:03:49.009 --> 00:03:51.109
and I do and I pray and

00:03:51.109 --> 00:03:56.049
I try to be led by the Lord, not every issue,

00:03:56.049 --> 00:04:01.349
I can't, you know, I, I can't find an answer to every issue in the scriptures. I mean, you know,

00:04:01.349 --> 00:04:02.280
the far right

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:03.140
they loved to,

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:06.519
the moral majority, they used to love to do a voting record

00:04:06.519 --> 00:04:10.659
on congressmen.

00:04:10.659 --> 00:04:12.939
And they, they always had ten votes every year

00:04:12.939 --> 00:04:14.959
and this is the far

00:04:14.959 --> 00:04:17.120
evangelical right and

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:20.329
out of ten votes I always maybe got three right,

00:04:20.329 --> 00:04:21.669
so therefore

00:04:21.669 --> 00:04:24.110
because I only vote thirty percent of the time,

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:26.199
I can't be a Christian.

00:04:26.199 --> 00:04:30.130
But I'm looking at some of their issues, you know, one of the issues was

00:04:30.130 --> 00:04:31.830
corporation franchise tax

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:33.159
and I'm thinking

00:04:33.159 --> 00:04:36.810
I'm looking in the scriptures for what Jesus says about the corporation franchise,

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:39.179
I can find it

00:04:39.179 --> 00:04:41.569
and so that,

00:04:41.569 --> 00:04:42.919
that gets back to

00:04:42.919 --> 00:04:44.580
one of the issues you said that,

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:48.850
you know, you can use religion in such a way that it's so odious

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:52.960
that it turns people off of God

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:55.800
and that those, those are some of the things that are being done

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:59.649
in American politics

00:04:59.649 --> 00:05:00.789
and a lot of other places.

